.         
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H2
.         * Our model is a fixed effects panel regression estimating how having
>  a daughter relates to left-leaning political preferences over time.
.         * Standard errors are clustered at the household level.
.         * Dependent variable: leftism - continuous index measuring left-leani
> ng political preferences (see above)
.         * Key predictor: has_daughter - whether the household has at least on
> e daughter in a given year
.         * Controls: whether the household has any children (has_child), age (
> age), age squared (age2), and number of sons and daughters (numbersons, numbe
> rdaughters).
. 
.         xtreg leftism has_daughter has_child age age2 numbersons numberdaught
> ers, fe cluster(cid)

